b6f611b-31ec-5ad6-9698-7aba48a1a8d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342306" :question/problem "$$\n({x}^{2}-4){y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The functions $P(x)=\\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}-4}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}-4}$ are analytic about $x=2.$\n- The functions $(x-2)P(x)$ and $(x-2)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=2.$\n- The point $x=2$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $x=a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $({x}^{2}-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-4){y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}-4}{y}^{′}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}-4}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}-4}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}-4}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=2,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=2.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x-2)P(x)=(x-2)\\cdot \\frac{5x}{{x}^{2}-4}=\\frac{5x}{x+2}\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=2,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}Q(x)=(x-2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}-4}=\\frac{(x-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{x+2}\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=2.$ Therefore, statement II is true.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=2$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is true, it follows that $x=2$ is a **regular** singular point. Thus, statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342306/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342306"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "93499243-4600-582e-8f7e-f01cf3f41a36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "ff2c4ad0-e7a4-54c0-aec3-16f7c37daad4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8ea1e8c9-77a2-58dd-b914-87e05eaf1a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "621efa39-45b1-5d37-bfe4-751f242d2a59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1f12d821-901a-5a55-8410-84eb18684485" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aed75b49-d600-5c51-adee-4f42f69349b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342307/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-342307/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-342307/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-342307/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-342307/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342307" :question/id #uuid "a478395d-5888-5691-9b70-b1f926c9a6c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-342307" :question/problem "$$\n(x+2){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x+2}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{3}}$ are analytic about $x=-2.$\n- The functions $(x+2)P(x)$ and $(x+2)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-2.$\n- The point $x=-2$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2){y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x+2}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{3}}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=-2,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=-2.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x+2)P(x)=(x+2)\\frac{1}{x+2}=1\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=-2,$ while the function\n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}Q(x)=(x+2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{(x+2)^{3}}=\\frac{1}{x+2}\n$$\n\nis *not* analytic about $x=-2$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=-2.$ Therefore, statement II is false.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=-2$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is false, it follows that $x=-2$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342307/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342307"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "800afd5e-ef98-52f7-b995-af257074338d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "80768076-c326-5655-8f02-657706f102ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "96bb5f65-c79e-5a0a-9adc-4c2d7d677226" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "836ec4a8-77f0-5bd8-acee-99b1169eca01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "99cc7404-a637-54dc-b826-4c6242067085" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d32288de-24b1-51e4-92e9-3d727d2a0769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342369/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342369/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-342369/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-342369/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-342369/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-342369/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342369" :question/id #uuid "1a5a8137-5abd-59c8-8d57-52f5cffa1a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-342369" :question/problem "$$\n(x-4){y}^{″}+\\frac{2}{x-4}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The functions $P(x)=\\frac{2}{(x-4)^{2}}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{3}}$ are analytic about $x=4.$\n- The functions $(x-4)P(x)$ and $(x-4)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=4.$\n- The point $x=4$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4){y}^{″}+\\frac{2}{x-4}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{2}}y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{2}{(x-4)^{2}}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{3}}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{2}{(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x-4)^{3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=4,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=4.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\n(x-4)P(x)=(x-4)\\cdot \\frac{2}{(x-4)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{x-4}\n$$\n\nis *not* analytic about $x=4,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x-4)^{2}Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x-4}\n$$\n\nis also *not* analytic about $x=4$ since its denominator vanishes at $x=4.$ Therefore, statement II is false.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=4$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is false, it follows that $x=4$ is an **irregular** singular point. Thus, statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342369/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-1/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" :answer/id #uuid "f64e6176-3081-5ff1-950e-90dac73d3aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-1/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" :answer/id #uuid "bf3f2b28-c51a-5833-979a-907f69cdc014" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-1/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answer/id #uuid "0e516e93-231b-5896-8e79-db7362f326f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d69d56ab-4ee0-5a15-9d3b-5efcf681ef96" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342416/field-1/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answer-field/choices ["q-342416/field-1/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" "q-342416/field-1/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" "q-342416/field-1/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-2/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" :answer/id #uuid "f647f787-ab99-5321-9af5-1673e196f1f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342416/field-2/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answe